# What each of Urdu's own characters arrives as: the code point a caller
# writes, and the byte its alphabet knows that character by.
#
# Most of them arrive as a letter Italian already has, so its own
# letter-to-sound rules apply to Urdu text unchanged and a word can be heard
# before a single rule has been written. Urdu writes one sound several ways --
# s three, z four -- and all of those arrive as the one letter, which costs
# telling them apart when spelling a word out and nothing when saying one.
#
# Five have a byte of their own, because a rule has to be able to see them
# and no Italian letter would say so: the three retroflexes, do chashmi he
# which makes the aspirates, and nun ghunna. Each says the nearest sound
# there is until the rule that says better is written.
#
# The letters and their sounds are from references/g2ps/Urdu, which is MIT.
# What is still wrong is in docs/notes/urdu.md: no aspirates, no retroflex
# sounds, no /h/, /x/ or /q/, no nasal vowels and no vowel length.

0621 68   # hamza -- the same
0622 61   # alef madda, long a
0627 61   # alef -- the vowel carrier, a
0628 62   # be
062a 74   # te, dental
062b 73   # se -- s
062c 89   # jim -- its own byte: g is a plain g before a
062d 68   # bari he -- h, which says nothing here
062e 6b   # khe -- k until there is an x
062f 64   # dal, dental
0630 7a   # zal -- z
0631 72   # re, a tap
0632 7a   # ze
0633 73   # sin
0634 8b   # shin -- its own byte: it was arriving as s
0635 73   # suad -- s
0636 7a   # zuad -- z
0637 74   # toe -- t as Urdu says it
0638 7a   # zoe -- z
0639 68   # ain -- silent, as h is here
063a 67   # ghain -- g
0641 66   # fe
0642 6b   # qaf -- k until there is a q
0644 6c   # lam
0645 6d   # mim
0646 6e   # nun
0648 75   # vao -- u, which is what it is oftenest
064e 61   # zabar, short a
064f 75   # pesh, short u
0650 69   # zer, short i
0679 82   # tte, retroflex -- its own byte, t until T sounds
067e 70   # pe
0686 88   # che -- its own byte: c is k before a in Italian
0688 83   # ddal, retroflex -- its own byte, d until D sounds
0691 84   # rre -- its own byte, the retroflex flap
0698 8d   # zhe -- its own byte, the voiced one of shin
06a9 6b   # kaf
06af 67   # gaf
06ba 87   # nun ghunna -- its own byte, no nasal vowels yet
06be 86   # do chashmi he -- its own byte, it makes the aspirates
06c1 68   # he -- the same
06cc 69   # ye -- i, which is what it is oftenest
06d2 65   # bari ye -- e
